+# Litha streaming render work
+
+The chat previously formatted and replaced every visible message on each streamed frame: four messages in Home and 60 in the dock. It also rebuilt unchanged suggestion/file rows and always scrolled to the bottom.
+
+Each view now retains rows for its current message window. New or removed messages reconcile the child list; changed content or terminal flags update that message's existing row. Settled message nodes remain in place during streaming, and unchanged file/suggestion HTML is not reassigned. The current reply is still formatted as a whole so partial code fences keep the existing formatting behavior. HTML-only hosts retain the former rendering path when a child-node API is unavailable.
+
+Streaming follows the bottom when the reader was already within 32 pixels of it. A reader looking higher keeps that scroll position. A new question requests bottom-following; zero-height/hidden lists are not programmatically scrolled. Composer nodes, drafts and composer text selections are not replaced. The active reply's HTML still changes; this does not preserve selections inside that changing reply. Native browser layout, selection and scrolling still require the integrator's visual review.
+
+An `incomplete` terminal event preserves formatted partial text and shows an escaped warning. It ends the pending turn, invalidates queued callbacks and marks the assistant fragment as an error so it is excluded from later model history. It does not automatically continue, apply code or claim tests ran. Generic errors retain their previous replacement behavior; cancelled replies keep their stopped label.
+
+## Local operation counts
+
+The optional comparison used the exact production module from commit `79489ad`, stored as an ignored local baseline file. Both implementations ran against the same inert DOM with 200 synthetic settled messages, Home/dock views, 100 streamed frames and a terminal flush. Initialization and the question's initial render precede the counter window.
+
+| Measured operation | Prior production | Current |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Settled-message formatter calls | 3,030 | 0 |
+| Whole message-list replacements | 202 | 0 |
+| HTML assignments, including file/suggestion rows | 606 | 200 |
+| Assigned HTML string length, UTF-16 code units | 4,268,940 | 78,890 |
+
+These are observed JavaScript/DOM API operation counts, not browser parsing, wall-clock, GPU, model latency or reasoning-quality measurements. The inert DOM does not parse `innerHTML` into native nodes. No speed multiplier or model-quality improvement is established.
+
+## Verification
+
+`node scripts/verify_litha_render_efficiency.mjs` passed 129 checks. It exercises actual production rendering with child-node identity, bounded row windows, drafts/selection, reader scrolling, hidden views, context updates, remounts, cancellation, errors, escaped code/warnings, incomplete fragments and history exclusion. Its default run needs no Git history, baseline file, browser, model or network.
+
+`node scripts/verify_litha_render_efficiency.mjs --baseline build/litha-render-baseline-79489ad.mjs` passed 132 checks and produced the comparison above. The optional argument must name the trusted prior production module; the verifier imports that module without starting the app.
+
+Existing standalone chat (59), Grid mount (14), main hooks (14), portrait lifecycle (61), portrait framing (59), and nine existing JavaScript checks passed unchanged. These selections overlap and are not an aggregate acceptance total. Node syntax checks passed. No existing tests, evaluation fixtures, portrait code, image assets or model prompts were edited by this lane.
